{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines","id":942768,"title":"Beat Engines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-03T09:45:19-07:00","id":942768,"title":"Beat Engines","content":"I\u2019ve been looking for good beat engines in Mage the Awakening. I think I\u2019ve found a really good one that I\u2019d like to share. I name this the Beat engine thread! Contributions welcome! Enjoy!<br /> <br /> I studied the Astral travel section in Mage the Awakening and found this little tidbit on p 250.<br /> <br /> Mages can return from their personal Oneiroi as a reflexive action. They just wake up. Coming back from anywhere else requires the same Resolve + Composure rolls for each Astral threshold, but doesn\u2019t require the mage to pass through vision challenges. She walks back along the now-resolved Astral Path. Alternately, she can deny herself full psychic reintegration with the material realm to wake up in a single turn, but leaving part of herself behind this way inflicts the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> Reading the Soul Shocked Condition on p 318 states that regaining all willpower ends the condition.<br /> <br /> The Clear Thoughts spell as a rote now becomes very useful to end the Soul Shocked condition and get an arcane beat.<br /> <br /> So as a character get Astral Adept meditate into the astral realms and snap back every single night. Heal willpower with Clear Thoughts and get a beat. I think to keep things fair characters should only be able to gain beats during a game session, otherwise a year of downtime turns into 73 arcane experience points. Sleep deprivation might also become an issue without some life magic. This potential for a beat engine makes having a demesne and a warlock with the Clear Thoughts rote very important to a cabal of mages.<br /> Any thoughts on this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T10:22:48-07:00","id":942793,"title":"","content":"Uh. Characters can ONLY gain Beats during a session. <br /> <br /> Also, I would never play with anyone who had a &quot;Beat engine&quot; clearly they are not interested in really playing the game, just scribbling numbers in their character sheet. <br /> <br /> You know what, I am going to do you a favor: I hereby grant you 1,000,000 Beats! All yours! If your ST doesn't believe me, just tell him to send a message my way. I got your back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:19:30-07:00","id":942828,"title":"","content":"You <i>are </i>meant to be able to intentionally inflict conditions on yourself with magic and resolve them as a means of growth, but the ST for a game where you tried this would be remiss if she didn't create some kind of consequence for doing it over and over. These aren't just numbers, you're repeatedly shredding your own consciousness for enlightenment. Conditions can emerge organically from gameplay in addition to being formally caused by specific triggers. If I had a PC do this, I'd probably start the Soul Loss condition track after they'd gotten 4 or 5 Beats out of it. It seems like a Wisdom sin in the same way as creating a soul stone too IMO, not that I'm a huge fan of using Wisdom punitively.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that you can only get 1 Beat per scene from resolving Conditions, so there are some pacing issues with any Condition-based &quot;engine.&quot; If you really want to spend your ~4 hours every 2 weeks (or however often your group plays) on grinding, be my guest, but surely actually using all those dots you bought would be more fun.<br /> <br /> Also also: c'mon dude, if you want to play a higher-level game, just tell your ST. You don't need to justify it with a rules loophole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:24:17-07:00","id":942832,"title":"","content":"I agree with arthexis, getting beats by the bucket load is not the objective of the game. However, the rules seem to let you do that. Honestly I feel like the ST should decide when you get beats instead of this &quot;Do X and you get a beat&quot;, but they didn't ask me how to design the game. I personally don't like beats because of it and have house ruled them out and basically it is just when I say you get beats, makes things much simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:32:34-07:00","id":942841,"title":"","content":"From the sidebar on pg 126, it's clear that it's intended for you to be able to cause conditions and resolve them specifically to earn beats. Having said that, there is the limit on how often you can do this (once per scene as others have mentioned), but also it's clear that it's supposed to be thematically appropriate. &quot;... mages do it all the time. Mastigos force their apprentices to face terrifying fears in order to better themselves... the only limits are the rule that a character may only earn one Beat per scene from resolving conditions, <b>and the limits of her own Wisdom</b>...&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd say it's certainly an act of Hubris and would bring Wisdom into it much sooner rather than later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:40:08-07:00","id":942852,"title":"","content":"The only &quot;Beat Engine&quot; I'd allow is some sort of Demonic Gadget that turns sound into electricity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:46:00-07:00","id":942856,"title":"","content":"Alright, I have a Beat Engine for everyone:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Beat Engine (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> This black basalt cube is about 3' on a side, with a circular depression on the &quot;top&quot;. If you pour water into the depression, one Mana is depleted from the cube's stores, and the cube starts to convert ambient temperature and sound into phat beats. Every sound within 100 meters is &quot;autotuned&quot;, delayed, echoed, or stretched in such a way that it produces a pleasant harmony, while the cube produces a thumping base beat that increases in complexity in line with ambient temperature. This effect automatically dissipates when the water in the depression is removed, which usually occurs due to evaporation.<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; <b>Gnosis</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022;<b> Mana:</b> 10","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 08-03-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:51:53-07:00","id":942866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=942841#post942841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the sidebar on pg 126, it's clear that it's intended for you to be able to cause conditions and resolve them specifically to earn beats. Having said that, there is the limit on how often you can do this (once per scene as others have mentioned), but also it's clear that it's supposed to be thematically appropriate. &quot;... mages do it all the time. Mastigos force their apprentices to face terrifying fears in order to better themselves... the only limits are the rule that a character may only earn one Beat per scene from resolving conditions, <b>and the limits of her own Wisdom</b>...&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd say it's certainly an act of Hubris and would bring Wisdom into it much sooner rather than later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is totally exploitable like a madman. Word of advice, don't let a Mage and Vampire make an arrangement of feeding.... That is a real beat Engine.<br /> #1. Addiction - Letting the Vampire drain your blood<br /> #2. Making an aspiration that leads to you hurting yourself to expose blood to enforce #1<br /> #3. Take a dramatic failure on the injury<br /> #4. Swooning - Do something for the Vampire<br /> #5. Do something questionable invoking a Wisdom sin as part of the Swooning (Meditate for a bonus +1 to Wisdom sin giving you a good solid 4 dice each time)<br /> #6. Make one of your aspirations revolving around one of these Swooning events.<br /> #7. Make your obsession related to the studying of Vampires and their habits.<br /> <br /> I had a player do that 3 times, never lost a point of Wisdom. He did other things to in order to get some more beats, he would end the night with roughly 10-11 beats. The reason he stopped was because he got tired of playing that character and made him an NPC.<br /> <br /> Easily 6-7 beats not including the other beats you can get from resolving condition and other story driven beats. You can do all that in 2 scenes and get 2 XP (+1 for playing) and it is repeatable and within the rules. After about 5 games you should have enough XP to get your Gnosis up 2 points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:13:07-07:00","id":942897,"title":"","content":"I totally agree it's still exploitable, just pointing out that the MtA book predicted this and explicitly called it out in the rulebook. Can you do it? Sure. There's even good IC reasons to do it. But it can and should affect your characters in a negative way to do it over and over again. I would increasingly penalize the wisdom roll every time, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:34:59-07:00","id":942957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=942897#post942897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally agree it's still exploitable, just pointing out that the MtA book predicted this and explicitly called it out in the rulebook. Can you do it? Sure. There's even good IC reasons to do it. But it can and should affect your characters in a negative way to do it over and over again. I would increasingly penalize the wisdom roll every time, but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't take long for the player to stop, but risking wisdom loss is another arcane beat...just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:40:28-07:00","id":942962,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's legitimate. 1E had a rule that you could give up Wisdom at character creation in exchange for Experiences. By contrast, now you can give up Wisdom for beats which are worth less than the experience points you got in 1E. <br /> <br /> If my player wants to give up Wisdom for beats, then I'm happy with that exchange but I would penalize them further and further each time. There's only so much you can learn by resolving the same condition over and over again in the same way, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T14:05:20-07:00","id":942980,"title":"","content":"You get a Beat whenever you -risk- Wisdom, not when you lose it. They don't have to lose any Wisdom to get it to keep generating Beats for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T14:24:50-07:00","id":942994,"title":"","content":"I mean, we can do the math on it. I would argue that knowingly taking on the risk of paradox as well as deleterious conditions constitutes a form of magical self mutilation which can take you down to 4 wisdom.<br /> <br /> For a hubris 6 act, you get 6 dice which give you roughly a 12% chance of failing your Wisdom roll, or an 88% of not losing any wisdom. You'll statistically be able to pull this off 6 times before losing a dot of wisdom. Six beats (1.2 experience) for that first wisdom dot. For hubris 5, the math comes out to 4 times (0.8 xp), and for hubris 4 acts this comes out to 3 tries before you're statistically likely to lose a dot.<br /> <br /> So, if you're OK with considering this an act of hubris down to Wisdom 4, your mage can trade 3 dots of Wisdom for an average of 2.6 experiences (13 beats). Of course, he may get more or less, but it would be statistically really unlikely (&lt;3% chance) for him to get more than four experiences (23 beats) out of this process.<br /> <br /> Assuming he also gets 1 beat per success for each condition resolved, this is looking at an average of 13x2=26 beats, with just as much chance of only getting 16 beats as 36. <br /> <br /> Is trading 3 wisdom (+ the time it takes given only once per scene) for 3-7 Experiences worth it? Maybe your player thinks so (or maybe my math is wrong!!).<br /> <br /> All in all this feels like much ado about nothing. Yes, technically this is all allowed by the game system but you'd have to have a pretty permissive storyteller and a pretty petty mage to see it happen, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":".  Forgot to factor in beats for resolving conditions. 08-03-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:22:13-07:00","id":943203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines#post942768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I\u2019ve been looking for good beat engines in Mage the Awakening</b>. I think I\u2019ve found a really good one that I\u2019d like to share. I name this the Beat engine thread! <b>Contributions welcome</b>! Enjoy!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I don't recall seeing the OP asking if you use beat engines, want to play in a game using them, or if you personally don't like using them in your game. If you don't like the thread topic and aren't going to contribute constructively then stay out of the thread. If you really feel the need go make your own thread about why you don't like beat engines, don't go shitting in someone else's thread. Pointing out a rules based limitation on how many beats can be generated per scene isn't threadcrapping, nor is pointing out other penalties the game may impose due to using a beat generating build. Just so we have some clear ground rules.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T22:01:10-07:00","id":943402,"title":"","content":"@Kvark: My hats off to you for the number crunching, I wouldn\u2019t have bothered, and thanks to Darksider for your ground rules. Actually thank you to everyone that responded. Let me pull back the curtain on what started me off on this rampage. <br /> <br /> When I read the thread about recharging mana and willpower by spamming praxis spells I was struck by how many people in the community seemed to be in support of taking advantage of a loophole in the rules to gain in character resources (mana and willpower). I have no problem with specific spells that do that. Knit and Mending heal hit points, Clarify Thoughts heals willpower and Essence Fountain heals mana (indirectly). I was fascinated by the idea that people wanted to replace Clarify Thoughts (Mind 3) and Essence Fountain (Spirit 5) with any old one dot spell that could be used to exploit the rules as written. The curiosity bug bit me and I asked \u201cHow far will this go?\u201d <br /> <br /> I always look over a game system as completely as I can, especially the experience/improvement portion. I had been considering how to advance a character quickly. Comparing the responses between the Praxis spamming thread and this thread I\u2019ve noticed a powerful split. The same community that largely supports dropping dramatic tension to exploit a loophole in the rules to grant a character in game resources also largely rejects the exploitation of a similar loophole to grant a character experience points (a meta game resource). <br /> <br /> <b>In short most people want their characters topped off at the expense of dramatic tension, but no one wants to see characters freely advance in power without participating in the story.</b><br /> <br /> I think between the two threads mentioned we\u2019ve uncovered a subject that should be explored further.<br /> <br /> As a final note the best experience engine is to attempt a roll with a poorly know skill or spell once per scene and volunteer a critical failure. That\u2019s the \u201cbeat engine\u201d that I would actually use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:25:35-07:00","id":943439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=943203#post943203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I don't recall seeing the OP asking if you use beat engines, want to play in a game using them, or if you personally don't like using them in your game. If you don't like the thread topic and aren't going to contribute constructively then stay out of the thread. If you really feel the need go make your own thread about why you don't like beat engines, don't go shitting in someone else's thread. Pointing out a rules based limitation on how many beats can be generated per scene isn't threadcrapping, nor is pointing out other penalties the game may impose due to using a beat generating build. Just so we have some clear ground rules.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is this comment directed towards me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T01:06:42-07:00","id":943479,"title":"","content":"It's directed at everyone, since too many people completely ignored the part in the original post where the OP asked people for ideas and to share their own versions of Beat engines and went straight into critic mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:06:48-07:00","id":943569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=943402#post943402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always look over a game system as completely as I can, especially the experience/improvement portion. I had been considering how to advance a character quickly. Comparing the responses between the Praxis spamming thread and this thread I\u2019ve noticed a powerful split. The same community that largely supports dropping dramatic tension to exploit a loophole in the rules to grant a character in game resources also largely rejects the exploitation of a similar loophole to grant a character experience points (a meta game resource).</div> </div> </div> </div>You sound like a QA tester <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I agree that these topics are definitely worth discussing, even if most people agree that most STs would shut down this behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=943402#post943402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>In short most people want their characters topped off at the expense of dramatic tension, but no one wants to see characters freely advance in power without participating in the story.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You hit the nail on the head. Like the math shows, it's not exactly freely advancing and it's not a huge advance. I'd argue that the 1E rule that let you trade Wisdom for experience points was much more powerful than the beat engine discussed here. You've also described a beat engine that has potentially cool in character ramifications, which is the best kind of &quot;gaming the system&quot; I could think of. It just depends on the ST adapting and rewarding/punishing accordingly.<br /> <br /> I mean, in my experience when my party wants more experience from an ST I ask for it, and they're happy to comply because ultimately it's about telling a story together and we wouldn't be asking for more experience unless we thought it could help us tell a richer story.<br /> <br /> I think people feel like beat engines are silly because the point of the beat system was for the game designers to set the *intended pace* for the experience economy. Otherwise, experience would simply be given at storyteller discretion (which is easy enough to house rule anyway). The beat system is far more new-player and new-ST friendly because it doesn't rely on an experienced storyteller knowing how fast to advance characters, but I can imagine most groups moving away from the system as soon as they hit their groove and get more experience under their belt as players and storytellers.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to seeing what other beat engines people come up with to see if they're similarly interesting ICly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:24:48-07:00","id":943578,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks Darksider for setting up the ground rules sir.<br /> <br /> My vampire example is probably the best one in terms of following by the rules that I have personally encountered and it was purely by accident. I am sure there are some more creative methods others can come up with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think people feel like beat engines are silly because the point of the beat system was for the game designers to set the *intended pace* for the experience economy. Otherwise, experience would simply be given at storyteller discretion (which is easy enough to house rule anyway). The beat system is far more new-player and new-ST friendly because it doesn't rely on an experienced storyteller knowing how fast to advance characters, but I can imagine most groups moving away from the system as soon as they hit their groove and get more experience under their belt as players and storytellers. </div> </div> </div>I agree with this statement, but the flip-side is it also leads to some interesting situations for experienced players that really just want to exploit the game for everything it is worth, which is probably where a lot of my knee-jerk reaction came from upon seeing this thread because I have ran into quite a few players that just want to exploit the system. So, my apologies.<br /> <br /> The best &quot;Beat Engine&quot; honestly, is play the game to have fun and make it easy for all involved.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T07:08:39-07:00","id":943594,"title":"","content":"Last session I got like 12 beats off Siskur Dah, rolling to summon, bind and stuck spirits into fetishes, then do the same process to get a spirit of secrets to translate a ciphered book. Failed once? Take the obsessive condition, take 9 again to rolls related to this task.<br /> <br /> Add Song in Your Heart and you're scoring exceptionals on 3s, getting a beat with each of those and having virtually inextinguishable WP.<br /> <br /> All the while being like 1 failure away of having an angry spirit at my pack's locus. High risk, high reward in a nutshell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-04-2016, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T07:12:11-07:00","id":943597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=943569#post943569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The beat system is far more new-player and new-ST friendly because it doesn't rely on an experienced storyteller knowing how fast to advance characters, but I can imagine most groups moving away from the system as soon as they hit their groove and get more experience under their belt as players and storytellers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree completely with this statement. The beat system is one of the best things to come out of the GMC. I can't think of any other mechanic more relevant to set the tone for a CoD game than beats. Sure, you may ignore them if you want, and in some circumstances I do so myself. However, whenever I do include them, the game feels more fun and focused, players stray less from the plot and when they do, they do so in dramatically interesting directions. It is hands down one of the best Experience systems I've seen (which isn't strange at all, since most XP systems are slowly moving in this direction, compare Dungeon World which is my seminal example for a lot of things).<br /> <br /> By the way, the Beats system is not really about character advancement. It kinda is, but that's not its main use. Using it just for that is a waste of its potential. Is it the perfect system? Nah, it just beats (pun intended) any other system that I've seen so far. Feel free to pose a counter-example, I would like to learn if anything better exists, honestly.<br /> <br /> Edit: I am certainly not a new ST in case you are wondering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:24:03-07:00","id":949385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=943402#post943402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same community that largely supports dropping dramatic tension to exploit a loophole in the rules to grant a character in game resources also largely rejects the exploitation of a similar loophole to grant a character experience points (a meta game resource).<br /> <br /> <b>In short most people want their characters topped off at the expense of dramatic tension, but no one wants to see characters freely advance in power without participating in the story.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I must admit, that has not been my impression of those threads. While I did get the feel of most people being disinclined to change the rules on the praxis-acquisition of willpower and mana, I did notice that most, if not all, were against this being exploited as a loophole, i.e. against a Mage spamming pretty lights to get mana, as it were.<br /> Rather the system was not seen as problematic ( not everyone agrees, I know XD ) due to insistence on in-character behavior that goes on with the plot and story and mood/theme rather than the proposed &quot;Gimme a few minutes, gotta drain some luck into Mana&quot; notion, meaning the system is fine as long as the exceptional successes are allowed to happen organically, from casting your praxis with at the very least a reasonable excuse. Outside of actual combat, you can get Mana in other reasonably convenient ways, so it's not too much of a drop in dramatic tension.<br /> <br /> As far as beats go, it is so far my favourite XP mechanic because it not only allows player agency in XP-acquisition in a narrative way, it also rewards story progression. All of the beat gains are things that are character development moments, if you choose to take them as such (which I do, ymmv) - a horrible failure that can stay with you for a while (dramatic failure), taking yet another step towards the megalomaniacal mage personality (Wisdom risk), experiencing the high of excellent spellcasting (exceptional success), these are all moments that can build a character.<br /> Doing one of those things over and over in the same way is not unlike someone developing an addiction to a feeling of heightened reality, what can be described as &quot;really being alive&quot; or &quot;feeling something,&quot; if the character is in a bad way.<br /> <br /> But I digress too much, for I have a Beat Engine to propose! (before I get into my convoluted one, a simple one is the condition sequence of Addicted -&gt; Deprived, then resolving Deprived)<br /> <br /> <b>What Doesn't Break You Makes You Stronger</b><br /> (and sometimes uses puns)<br /> <br /> In a never-talked-about area of the Adamantine Arrow compound there is a room with a non-descript door, within it lie two boxes, each an on altar, on opposite sides of the room.<br /> The room has no other entrances or exits, no windows. The boxes are illuminated with candles, providing the only light in the room, their surfaces large enough to place a hand on with fingers spread out.<br /> The box on the left side appears to be made of steel and inlaid with gold decorations and script, bearing depictions of double-edged swords, and the word BREAK.<br /> The box on the right apperas to be made of stone, inlaid with copper decorations and script, bearing depictions of axes, and the word RENEW.<br /> The walls are decorated with tapestries depicting Mages triumphant in a bloodied state.<br /> <br /> The room sees no use in times of conflict, when the Arrows are tempered through battle. But when times of peace come, the Adamantine Arrow knows the need to stay ready.To train, yes, but a keen awareness exists that sparring matches, or indeed anything, cannot fully prepare one for true battle.<br /> Nothing can do it fully, but you can get closer. In times of prolonged peace, Arrows who have never experienced battle, but will be expected to take up arms when the need arises - never quite newcomers, but those with some measure of growth shown - are ushered into the room with the non-descript door in the place nobody talks about.<br /> They are instructed to find strength in overcoming pain.<br /> The screams and shouting from the room are never commented upon by those standing guard outside, and those exiting do so with greater understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mechanics!<br /> Each of the boxes is an imbued item. They are both triggered by placing one's hand on the surface of the box. The left box contains a Forces effect that inflicts the Disabled Condition by breaking both of the target's legs. With all the pain that involves.<br /> The initiate then has to make their way across the room (by using their hands for movement) to trigger the second box.<br /> The right box contains a Life effect that heals some damage and cures the Disabled Condition by unbreaking the legs, as it were.<br /> There we go, Condition, resolved, take a Beat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=943402#post943402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a final note the best experience engine is to attempt a roll with a poorly know skill or spell once per scene and volunteer a critical failure. That\u2019s the \u201cbeat engine\u201d that I would actually use.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of course, if you really want into optimisation, and I don't see why not as long as you also make it interesting in-character behavior that's fun for the group, make use of eeeeverything that gives beats.<br /> In every scene, get and resolve a condition (or 'take a beat from exceptional success' if the ST rules that way), dramatically fail on a roll in a dramatic way (that will get you a reputation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), risk Wisdom and portray the subsequent introspection from that, and try to make some progress on an Obsession whenever remotely possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","user":"Aeryes","date":".  Typos 08-13-2016, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:09:25-07:00","id":949911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines#post942768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the Soul Shocked Condition on p 318 states that regaining all willpower ends the condition.<br /> <br /> The Clear Thoughts spell as a rote now becomes very useful to end the Soul Shocked condition and get an arcane beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I don't believe that's rules-legal unless you get a critical success on the Clear Thoughts spell. While it's not explicitly stated, I think it's a pretty direct extrapolation to draw from these two rules on page 126.<br /> <br /> &quot;Spells can mimic the effects of a helpful Condition, but using magic to gain a benefit and a Beat is double-dipping. Beneficial Conditions created by magic don\u2019t grant Beats unless they\u2019re the result of an exceptional success.&quot;<br /> &quot;Removing a condition with magic is always at least a Ruling (\u2022\u2022) spell, but otherwise follows the same guidelines as creating one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Since using magic to gain a benefit and a beat is prohibited in spells that provide a condition and spells that remove a condition follow the same rules, therefore Clear Thoughts should not be able to provide a benefit (regaining willpower) and a beat (from resolving the condition) unless you roll a critical success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T02:48:35-07:00","id":949951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=949911#post949911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I don't believe that's rules-legal unless you get a critical success on the Clear Thoughts spell. While it's not explicitly stated, I think it's a pretty direct extrapolation to draw from these two rules on page 126.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Spells can mimic the effects of a helpful Condition, but using magic to gain a benefit and a Beat is double-dipping. Beneficial Conditions created by magic don\u2019t grant Beats unless they\u2019re the result of an exceptional success.&amp;quot;<br /> &amp;quot;Removing a condition with magic is always at least a Ruling (\u2022\u2022) spell, but otherwise follows the same guidelines as creating one.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Since using magic to gain a benefit and a beat is prohibited in spells that provide a condition and spells that remove a condition follow the same rules, therefore Clear Thoughts should not be able to provide a benefit (regaining willpower) and a beat (from resolving the condition) unless you roll a critical success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's one step below explicit. The +2 reach option does exactly say that it resolves conditions as a lasting effect and that doing so does not grant beats. This means by implication that the clear thoughts spell does not resolve conditions without reaching, and that doing so will not grant you beats. The purpose of that spell is to give you back the mental capacity that you need to function, not to instantly give the understanding and &quot;wisdom&quot; of what caused the condition and why moving past it was important. <br /> <br /> That being said, I'm not interested in a beat engine for the same reason that I don't just simply purchase the Egregore merit with the xp I've gained: I personally want to enjoy the real life experience of earning those beats from playing the game. I'm interested in the benefits of the Egregore merit, but I'm even more interested in role playing those initiations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T03:55:30-07:00","id":949968,"title":"","content":"Not that I care to much about this subject anymore because the question behind my question is answered but at Michael Kenner what I meant was that Clear Thoughts helps recover willpower with a reach effect. When you get all your willpower back the Soul Shocked condition ends. I wasn't thinking about it just being removed. Anyway people don't like beat engines, that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T04:04:06-07:00","id":949970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=949911#post949911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don't believe that's rules-legal unless you get a critical success on the Clear Thoughts spell. While it's not explicitly stated, I think it's a pretty direct extrapolation to draw from these two rules on page 126.<br /> &quot;Spells can mimic the effects of a helpful Condition, but using magic to gain a benefit and a Beat is double-dipping. Beneficial Conditions created by magic don\u2019t grant Beats unless they\u2019re the result of an exceptional success.&quot;<br /> &quot;Removing a condition with magic is always at least a Ruling (\u2022\u2022) spell, but otherwise follows the same guidelines as creating one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Since using magic to gain a benefit and a beat is prohibited in spells that provide a condition and spells that remove a condition follow the same rules, therefore Clear Thoughts should not be able to provide a benefit (regaining willpower) and a beat (from resolving the condition) unless you roll a critical success.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Falcon777's post on the Reach option of Clear Thoughts does, ahem, clarify the situation, I disagree that your logic would otherwise apply here.<br /> The text you quote deals specifically with spells that give a Condition that you then resolve, and give the ruling that such resolution does not grant a Beat.<br /> <br /> To me, it does not follow that any and all resolution of Conditions by means of spells cannot allow Beat acquisition. That would go just for beneficial spell-acquired Conditions. <br /> <br /> There's another piece of text whose location eludes me where it mentions that removing Conditions by means of spells does not resolve Conditions and thus does not grant Beats. But this is also a different matter to using magic to meet a negative Condition's resolve condition. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T04:54:26-07:00","id":949982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Servanous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=949968#post949968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I care to much about this subject anymore because the question behind my question is answered but at Michael Kenner what I meant was that Clear Thoughts helps recover willpower with a reach effect. When you get all your willpower back the Soul Shocked condition ends. I wasn't thinking about it just being removed. Anyway people don't like beat engines, that's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't really read the majority of the thread since it seemed off topic. I just wanted to reply to the scenario you set out and stick to the facts.<br /> <br /> The point you make is certainly a valid argument, I'm not sure that I agree personally but it does make sense. Since the spell is deliberately being cast for the purpose of removing a condition and applying a beat, I think that the rules for spells to achieve those effects should apply. Especially given that it's the immediate result and the intervening steps only occur on paper (the character sheet) without any narrative events occurring within the story. However, that largely just comes down to personal opinion and interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=949970#post949970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Falcon777's post on the Reach option of Clear Thoughts does, ahem, clarify the situation, I disagree that your logic would otherwise apply here.<br /> The text you quote deals specifically with spells that give a Condition that you then resolve, and give the ruling that such resolution does not grant a Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might have missed part of what I wrote there. I quoted two pieces of rules text, one referring to the other and you're only mentioning the first. I'll paraphrase them for simplicity but I wanted to use the whole text to prove it was there.<br /> <br /> Rule 1. A spell that gives you conditions shouldn't give you a benefit and a beat.<br /> Rule 2. A spell that removes conditions works in all ways like a spell that gives you a condition.<br /> :. Extrapolated rule. A spell that removes conditions shouldn't give you a benefit and a beat.<br /> <br /> (I removed the part about critical successes for clarity there).<br /> <br /> However I think you're right and there is another part of the book that says the rule you're talking about, I remember seeing it once when I was reading the book but I can't remember where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:55:14-07:00","id":950206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=949982#post949982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might have missed part of what I wrote there. I quoted two pieces of rules text, one referring to the other and you're only mentioning the first. I'll paraphrase them for simplicity but I wanted to use the whole text to prove it was there.<br /> <br /> Rule 1. A spell that gives you conditions shouldn't give you a benefit and a beat.<br /> Rule 2. A spell that removes conditions works in all ways like a spell that gives you a condition.<br /> :. Extrapolated rule. A spell that removes conditions shouldn't give you a benefit and a beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not miss what you wrote, I didn't agree with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I may have been unclear though. (and potentially just wrong XD)<br /> <br /> The syllogism you list works rather nicely, but my point was that it doesn't neccessarily come into play.<br /> Your version: Spell removes Condition, syllogism says no Beat. We agree there.<br /> My version (and I think Servanous' too) : Spell does an effect and ends, the effect also makes the Condition resolve. Resolution grants the Beat.<br /> <br /> Might be nitpicky? Is on shaky grounds for some Conditions? Sure. (I don't think it is for my example Beat Engine as the Condition allows for magical curing of the disability as resolution explicitly)<br /> <br /> The intent of the spell could be to remove the Condition, but it's not what the effect does, both for Soul Shocked and for Disabled. For the first, the spell recovers willpower. For the second, the spell heals the injury. Is the difference from directly removing Soul Shocked or Disabled significant enough? To me it is. Mileages may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:13:56-07:00","id":950240,"title":"","content":"I'd say a spell that makes a Condition resolve should make it grant a Beat, as long as the Condition wasn't caused by a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:50:17-07:00","id":950311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942768-beat-engines?p=950206#post950206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not miss what you wrote, I didn't agree with it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I may have been unclear though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine. Just reading the first reply you wrote, it seemed to only mention the first rule. Since what I was saying relied on both rules in tandem to make sense, I needed to make sure you were disagreeing with what I was saying and not disagreeing with something different that I hadn't intended to convey.<br /> <br /> Now that you've expanded on it, much as with Servanous, I think your argument is an entirely valid interpretation. Not one that I personally hold myself, but it does make complete sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}